<!--
  The Six Day Stilt, made more of a market.

  The idea and the two new merchants are Mura's, from the Caves of Qud Expanded - The Grand Bazaar
  sub-mod, absorbed under the permission recorded in docs/PERMISSION.md §9. **The numbers are not
  his.** That mod raises merchant stock about 1.68x overall and reaches tier 8; this is held to
  1.3x per table and stops at tier 6, so roughly three quarters of what it added is not here. See
  #174 for the derivation and docs/FEATURES.md for the reasoning.

  Its SixDayTents.cs does not travel. It declares vanilla's own type name and has therefore never
  run for anybody (#775), and repointing the builder would mean replacing vanilla's whole
  SixDayStilt cell, which charter rule 1 refuses (#793).

  Every vanilla record here is a merge. A child that *changes* a vanilla value carries its own
  Load="Merge" - without it the child appends and both rows roll, which is the duplication trap
  #798 recorded.
-->
<populations>
  <!-- ============================================================ Mura's two merchants and tents -->

