  </population>

  <population Name="Vixy_PedlarTentContents">
    <group Name="Contents" Style="pickeach">
      <object Blueprint="Vixy_Pedlar" Number="1" Hint="Interior" />
      <object Blueprint="Woven Basket" Number="1-2" Hint="AlongInsideWall" />
    </group>
  </population>

  <!-- ============================================================================ vanilla merges -->

  <!--
    Two more tent kinds. StiltTents is a pickone, so adding weight dilutes every existing entry
    without touching anybody's number - and an empty tent goes from 5.0% to 4.5% of tents as a
    side-effect, which is the honest way to have fewer of them. Weight 4 matches what vanilla gives
    its own ordinary merchant tents.
  -->
  <population Name="StiltTents" Load="Merge">
    <group Name="Types" Load="Merge">
      <table Name="Raven_SmithyTent" Weight="4" />
      <table Name="Raven_WaterMerchantTent" Weight="4" />
    </group>
  </population>

  <!--
    An unclaimed stall is somebody with not much to sell, rather than eight to twelve bedrolls,
    which is what the Grand Bazaar put here. Vanilla's EmptyTent holds one table; this adds a person
    beside it and takes nothing away.

    Note the weight of EmptyTent itself is left alone. It could be merged down to 2 or 3 - but not
    to 1, because PopulationItem.MergeFrom reads `if (Item.Weight != 1)`, so a merged weight of
    exactly one is silently discarded. Adding a merchant is additive and needs no such trick.
  -->
  <population Name="EmptyTent" Load="Merge">
    <group Name="Contents" Load="Merge">
      <table Name="Vixy_PedlarTentContents" />
    </group>
  </population>

